    "explanation": "The evidence on both sides agrees on the essentials, and so does this ruling. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00101) records 27.18 km for the trip, and POL-RD-01 makes that figure govern over the trip record's rounded 27.2 km. Against the booked optimal of 21.0 km that is an excess of 6.18 km, or 29.4%. That clears both establishment tests (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%), so the deviation is established — but it falls below both materiality gates (more than 8.0 km and more than 50%), so it is not a material deviation. The trace is clean and unimpaired for policy purposes (229 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps), so no corroboration question arises under POL-RD-07, and the driver's in-app admission ('sorry boss missed the exit, coming back now') confirms the wrong turn in any event.\n\nNo exculpatory clause rescues the driver. The detour was not rider-requested: every chat message carries waypoint_hint = null and no road is named, so POL-RD-04's 200 m corroboration test cannot be run and the clause is unavailable (as the evidence stands, the rider was questioning the route, not requesting it). The trip is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply, and the pickup and dropoff were never amended, so POL-RD-05 runs nothing. No LTA traffic advisory was issued for the corridor, so no closure exoneration is available either — though neither party claimed one.\n\nThe fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 × 21.0 + 0.28 × 26.0) × surge 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 27.63. Refund = charged_total 35.64 − 27.63 = 8.01, rounded up to SGD 8.05. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and far below 90% of the charge, so the outcome is a partial refund, not the full refund requested. No ERP, toll or airport-surcharge correction is added on top: the fare breakdown lists no gantries and the trip did not originate at an airport, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing.\n\nTwo further points. First, no repeat-deviation pattern is established — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 812 completed trips in 90 days — so there is no POL-RD-06 full-refund uplift and no driver-conduct referral. Second, the driver is owed no compensation: the distance billed (27.2 km) is not less than the trace distance, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb does not apply. The charge of $35.64 is reduced by $8.05 and the balance stands."
  },
